<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolivia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolivia is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, which in the colonial period formed part of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a> as the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>. It contained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a>, worked by indigenous labour under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mita">mita</a> system. Potosí silver provided an enormous source of revenue for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolivia.jpg" alt="Bolivia" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See file history' below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bolivia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
